---
layout: default
---
{%- comment -%}
  Home page of the doctoral portfolio (krunalpanchalphd.github.io). A short, focused alternative to the
  Studio-centred `home` layout: intro and research philosophy, the end-to-end loop, project tiles, selected publications.
  Text comes from the same data files as the rest of the site (intake_pages.about, socials, projects).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ab = site.data.intake_pages.about -%}
{%- assign soc = site.data.socials -%}
{%- assign phil = ab.body_md | split: '## Research philosophy' | last | split: '## Background' | first | strip -%}
{%- assign projs = site.projects | sort: 'importance' -%}
<div class="home phd-home">
  <section class="home-intro" id="about" aria-label="Introduction">
    <p class="eyebrow">Doctoral research portfolio</p>
    <h1 class="phd-home__name">Dr. Krunal R. Panchal</h1>
    <p class="home-cred mono">
      <span>PhD, Mechanical Engineering, IIT Madras ({{ ab.extra.degree_year }})</span>
      <span>Process engineering for reacting systems: chemistry, uncertainty, CFD, and machine-learning surrogates</span>
    </p>
    <div class="home-pull">{{ phil | markdownify }}</div>
    <div class="home-dock">
      <ul class="home-cta" aria-label="Main sections">
        <li><a class="btn-cta btn-cta-primary" href="{{ '/projects/mosiac/' | relative_url }}">The MOSIAC loop</a></li>
        <li><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/projects/' | relative_url }}">Projects</a></li>
        <li><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/playground/' | relative_url }}">Neural-ODE playground</a></li>
        <li><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">Publications</a></li>
        <li><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/about/' | relative_url }}">About</a></li>
        <li><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/cv/' | relative_url }}">CV</a></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="home-links" aria-label="Profiles">
        {%- if soc.github_username -%}<li><a href="https://github.com/{{ soc.github_username }}" rel="me noopener"><i class="fa-brands fa-github" aria-hidden="true"></i>GitHub</a></li>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if soc.orcid_id -%}<li><a href="https://orcid.org/{{ soc.orcid_id }}" rel="me noopener"><i class="ai ai-orcid" aria-hidden="true"></i>ORCID</a></li>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if soc.linkedin_username -%}<li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/{{ soc.linkedin_username }}" rel="me noopener"><i class="fa-brands fa-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></i>LinkedIn</a></li>{%- endif -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-sec" aria-labelledby="phd-loop">
    <header class="home-sec__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How the work fits together</p>
      <h2 id="phd-loop">One loop, from building a model to using it</h2>
    </header>
    <p>
      The same six steps run through everything here, in the order of Bloom's revised taxonomy: remember the chemistry, understand what
      controls it, apply it in simulation, analyse the uncertainty, evaluate it against experiments, and create something new from it.
      <a href="{{ '/projects/mosiac/' | relative_url }}">MOSIAC</a> is that loop for combustion chemistry; the last step, running the
      calibrated model inside CFD and teaching a neural network to stand in for it, is current research.
    </p>
    <ol class="phd-loop">
      <li><b>Construct</b> <span>build or import the reaction mechanism</span></li>
      <li><b>Explain</b> <span>which reactions control which measurements</span></li>
      <li><b>Simulate</b> <span>reactors, flames, cross-checked solvers</span></li>
      <li><b>Quantify and reduce</b> <span>how sure are we; keep only what matters</span></li>
      <li><b>Calibrate</b> <span>tune against experiments with honest error bars</span></li>
      <li><b>Use</b> <span>CFD and Neural-ODE surrogates (current research)</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="home-sec" aria-labelledby="phd-projects">
    <header class="home-sec__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Work</p>
      <h2 id="phd-projects"><a href="{{ '/projects/' | relative_url }}" class="about-h2-link">Projects</a></h2>
    </header>
    <div class="phd-tiles">
      {%- for p in projs -%}
        <a class="phd-tile raised" href="{{ p.url | relative_url }}">
          {%- if p.img -%}<img src="{{ p.img | relative_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{%- endif -%}
          <span class="phd-tile__t">{{ p.title | escape }}</span>
          <span class="phd-tile__d">{{ p.description | truncate: 150 | escape }}</span>
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- if page.selected_papers -%}
    {%- capture sel_count -%}{% bibliography_count --query @*[selected=true]* %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign sel_n = sel_count | strip | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if sel_n > 0 -%}
      <section class="home-sec" aria-labelledby="home-pubs">
        <header class="home-sec__head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Papers</p>
          <h2 id="home-pubs"><a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}" class="about-h2-link">Selected publications</a></h2>
        </header>
        {% include selected_papers.liquid %}
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
<style>
  .phd-home__name { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); margin: 0.2em 0 0.3em; }
  .phd-loop { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(175px, 1fr)); list-style: none; padding: 0; counter-reset: s; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .phd-loop li { counter-increment: s; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.35)); border-radius: 10px; }
  .phd-loop li::before { content: counter(s); display: inline-block; width: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; opacity: 0.55; }
  .phd-loop span { display: block; font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.8; }
  .phd-tiles { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); }
  .phd-tile { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.8rem; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.35)); border-radius: 12px; }
  .phd-tile img { width: 100%; height: 150px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 8px; }
  .phd-tile__t { font-weight: 700; }
  .phd-tile__d { font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.8; }
</style>
